        },
        "text_founder_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Kim Gravel</strong> has built an extraordinary career across many chapters — <strong>Miss Georgia, television personality, motivational speaker, author, businesswoman, and QVC host</strong> — and through every single one, her <strong>core message</strong> has always been the same: <strong>you are enough, exactly as you are.</strong></p><p>She first stepped into the national spotlight as Miss Georgia, then spent decades reaching millions of women across stages, screens, and living rooms with a truth she refused to stop telling. <strong>You are worthy. You are beautiful. You are enough.</strong></p><p><strong>LWYA is the natural extension of everything Kim has always stood for.</strong> After years on television watching women shrink themselves, apologize for taking up space, and hide behind the wrong beauty products, Kim decided to build something different.</p><p><strong>A brand that starts not with what you lack, but with who you already are.</strong> She created LWYA because <strong>she believes every woman deserves beauty products that actually work, a community that actually sees her, and a daily reminder that loving yourself is not selfish.</strong> It is essential.</p><p>LWYA is Kim's love letter to every woman who has ever stood in front of a mirror and needed someone to remind her she was beautiful. Consider this your reminder.</p>",
            "text_custom": false,
            "text_font": "josefin_sans_n4",
            "text_size": 25,
            "text_size_mobile": 16,
            "text_height": 150,
            "text_mt": 16,
